-- title:
--   Automorphic induction of a ray class symbol to weight one
-- statement:
--   Let $E \subseteq M$ be number fields with $[M:E]=2$, let $\mathfrak f \neq 0$ be an ideal of $\mathcal O_M$, let $\psi$ assign a unit of $\mathbb C$ to every finite place of $M$, and let $\varepsilon$ assign a unit of $\mathbb C$ to every real embedding $\varphi\colon M \to \mathbb R$. Assume: (i) for every non-zero $\alpha \in \mathcal O_M$ with $\alpha - 1 \in \mathfrak f$, the ray symbol $\prod_{w} \psi(w)^{\operatorname{count}_w(\alpha \mathcal O_M)}$ (a finite product over the finite places of $M$, the exponent being the valuation of the fractional ideal generated by $\alpha$) equals $\prod_{\varphi(\alpha)<0}\varepsilon(\varphi)$, the product over the real embeddings negative on $\alpha$; (ii) $\varepsilon(\varphi)\varepsilon(\varphi') = -1$ for all distinct real embeddings $\varphi \neq \varphi'$ of $M$ agreeing on $E$; (iii) there are distinct finite places $w' \neq w''$ of $M$ lying over one and the same place of $E$, neither of whose prime ideals divides $\mathfrak f$, with $\psi(w') \neq \psi(w'')$. Let further $c,u,d_1,d_2$ be reals with $c>0$ and $d_1>0$, and let $T$ be a finite set of elements of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A_E)$. Then there is a Hecke eigensystem $\Psi$ over $E$ with values in $\mathbb C$, that is, a non-zero level ideal of $\mathcal O_E$ together with eigenvalue functions $\Psi.a, \Psi.b$ on the finite places of $E$, such that: first, for the carrier data `productionPinsOf` built from the Borel measurable structure and Haar measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A_E)$, the full central subgroup, the domain $D = \bigcup_{x \in T} \{g x : g \in \mathrm{centreCutSiegelSet}\,E\,c\,u\,d_1\,d_2\}$ (right translates by $T$ of the set of $g$ whose finite part is integral, whose archimedean local heights are all $\geq c$, whose $x$-windows satisfy $\mathrm{xWindowSq} \leq u^2$ and whose archimedean determinant norms lie in $[d_1,d_2]$), the level subgroups $N \mapsto \mathrm{levelOne}(N) \cap \ker(\mathrm{glArch})$, the Hecke generators $v \mapsto \mathrm{heckeGen}\,v$, and the conditioned additive Haar measure on the adelic box, there exists a smooth cusp realisation $R$ of the recentred eigensystem $\Psi.\mathrm{toRawCentral}$ (the same level and $a$, with $b$ replaced by $v \mapsto (\mathrm{cNorm}\,v)^{-1}\Psi.b\,v$) whose underlying function $R.\mathrm{toFun}$ is continuous, transforms at every real place $w$ of $E$ under the predicate `HasArchCharacterAt₀` by the weight-one character $\mathrm{archWeightOneAt}\,h_w$ (the standard weight-one character of the row-isometry subgroup of $\mathbb R$, transported along the identification of the completion at $w$ with $\mathbb R$), and is archimedean-holomorphic at every real place $w$, i.e. for every $g$ the function $z \mapsto (\operatorname{Im} z)^{-1} R.\mathrm{toFun}(g \cdot \iota_w(\mathrm{iwasawaSectionGL}\,z))$ is differentiable on the upper half-plane; secondly, there is a finite set $S$ of finite places of $E$ such that for every $w \notin S$, whenever $w' \neq w''$ are distinct places of $M$ both lying over $w$ one has $\Psi.a\,w = \psi(w') + \psi(w'')$ and $\Psi.b\,w = \psi(w')\psi(w'')$, and whenever $w'$ lies over $w$ with inertia degree $\mathrm{inertiaDeg}'$ equal to $2$ one has $\Psi.a\,w = 0$ and $\Psi.b\,w = -\psi(w')$.
--
--   This is automorphic induction from $\mathrm{GL}_1$ over $M$ to $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over $E$ for a quadratic extension in holomorphic weight one: the eigensystem $\Psi$ is the theta series attached to the ray class character of $M$ whose values at primes are tabulated by $\psi$ and whose signs at the real places are $\varepsilon$, the displayed eigenvalue formulae being the split, and inert, cases of the induced Frobenius trace and determinant. It is obtained by combining the construction of a finite-order Hecke character of $M$ from the ray symbol data with the corresponding statement for Hecke characters, and feeds the Langlands–Tunnell input [`LanglandsTunnell.exists_agreesAwayFromFinite_isGenuineCusp_of_raySymbol_eq_one`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.exists_agreesAwayFromFinite_isGenuineCusp_of_raySymbol_eq_one).
